<title>RUSSIA: Russia Mashinoimport signs for 16,000 bpd Iraq oil.</title>
<headline>Russia Mashinoimport signs for 16,000 bpd Iraq oil.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Mashinoimport oil trading company signed a contract on Friday with Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organisation (SOMO) for 400,000 tonnes of Iraqi crude over six months (about 16,000 barrels per day), a Russian oil executive said.</p>
<p>Yuri Agababov, deputy director of Zarubezhneft, which is coordinating all Russian purchases, said Russia's Rosneft and International Economic Cooperation, known as MES, were also in Baghdad for talks on contracts and could sign by Saturday.</p>
<p>He did not know from which outlet Mashinimport would lift the oil or the size of the two contracts still being negotiated.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
